                <text type="synoptic_situation">A ridge of high pressure moves into western SA and will persist over most the state, as the associated high drifts east across waters to the south, clearing east of Australia from Thursday. A trough and low pressure system are then forecast to track into western SA on Thursday before crossing the rest of the state on Friday.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
